1. DEFINITIONS
   "Seesaw" means this software: its source code, scripts, documentation and the artwork and sounds the copyright holder
   created for it, in every version that carries this licence.
   "Licensor" means unidotcon1, the copyright holder.
   "You" means the person or organisation that installs or runs Seesaw.
   "Evaluation Period" means the 60 consecutive days that begin the first time You start Seesaw on a computer.
   "Full Licence" means a licence file for Seesaw, signed by the Licensor, that names You (or Your organisation) and an end date.

2. EVALUATION GRANT
   During the Evaluation Period the Licensor grants You a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable
   licence to install, run and modify Seesaw on computers You control, for Your own personal use or the internal use of Your
   organisation, including running it at events You host.

3. WHEN THE EVALUATION ENDS
   When the Evaluation Period ends You must stop running Seesaw and delete Your copies, unless You hold a Full Licence.
   Photos taken with Seesaw belong to the people in them and to You; deleting Seesaw does not require deleting those photos.

4. FULL LICENCE
   A Full Licence replaces clause 3 for the period and scope written in the licence file. The Licensor may charge a fee or
   attach conditions to a Full Licence. A Full Licence is personal to the named licensee and cannot be passed on.

5. WHAT YOU MUST NOT DO
   a) Remove, disable, bypass or tamper with the licence check, the evaluation end date or the licence file verification
      (for example: deleting or editing the files that record the first start, changing the computer clock to gain days,
      editing the scripts or the Worker so the check no longer runs, or forging a licence file).
   b) Use Seesaw after the Evaluation Period without a Full Licence.
   c) Sell, rent, lease, host as a service for others, or sublicense Seesaw, or include it in a product You sell.
   d) Share Seesaw or a modified version of it with anyone else, except an unmodified copy of the complete package, including
      this licence, so that the recipient can evaluate it under these same terms. A recipient's own Evaluation Period starts
      when the recipient first runs it.
   e) Remove or change the copyright notices, this licence, or the credit in clause 6.
   f) Use Seesaw to break the law or to photograph or share pictures of people without their permission.

6. CREDIT
   Keep the notice "Seesaw by unidotcon1 - https://github.com/unidotcon1/Seesaw" visible in the documentation and wherever
   Seesaw shows its credit (the privacy dialog). If You publish photos or material that show Seesaw, a credit is appreciated.

7. OWNERSHIP
